# Automated Trading - Rules

## Global Rules Reference
Global rules are available in ~/.zed/rules/:
- system_env.md - CachyOS, fish, uv, podman standards
- python_standards.md - Type hints, async, error handling
- troubleshooting_protocol.md - Diagnostic-first troubleshooting
- socratic_mentor.md - Principal Architect persona

## Project-Specific Rules
See .zed/rules/trading_context.md for trading-specific patterns.

## Key Guidelines
- Always use Decimal for money calculations (never float)
- Enforce position limits before trades
- Validate ML predictions before execution
- Use UTC timestamps for all market data
- Log every order with full context
